{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And leave his father and die</b> Rabbi Abraham explained: \"and his father will die.\" If so, he should have said, \"Our father cannot leave his son,\" and \"he will leave his son and die,\" or \"we cannot allow the youth to leave his father,\" for they would not base the compassion on their father's feelings toward the youth, since they would hold on to him as a child who does not know between good and evil. Rather, the meaning of \"the youth cannot leave his father\" is because of his youth and his being a cherished child in the bosom of his father who loved him, and if he leaves him and goes on the journey, the youth will die."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:22:24.139695512Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}